# Design System: Folio3 Parking — Bay Control

## 1. Visual Theme & Atmosphere
A precise instrument panel for a corporate car park. It is used by employees on their phones, by guards at the barrier and by administrators at a desk all day. Surfaces are near-black and tinted towards the cyan accent in three steps. Structure comes from 1px low-alpha hairlines and inset rules, never shadows. Every number, plate, floor, time and code is set in mono with tabular figures. The mood is calm and watchful. It should read like a well-made dashboard instrument, never like science fiction.

- **Dials:** Density 7 ("Cockpit-leaning": compact rows, tight labels, fast to scan), Variance 4 (left-aligned, grid-true, mild asymmetry: content rail plus a detail column), Motion 7 (fast, exact and meaningful; nothing decorative).
- **Field reading:** Ticketmaster uses its blue only on actions and the seat-picker total. We do the same: the accent marks only the action, the selected item and the focus ring. SeatGeek pairs a bright cyan with a deep navy ground. We take that cyan-on-deep relationship and move it into dark mode. BMW is crisp and technical with sharp corners, so our corners are sharp (2–4px) and headings are medium weight, not heavy. Ford and Toyota keep owner screens plain. Our employee screens are equally plain: one key fact (a space, a floor, a plate) set large, with everything else quiet.
- **Field defaults changed:** light → dark mode (guards watch a live check and an alert must stand out). Comfortable → dense (administrators scan tables all day). Pure neutrals → cyan-tinted neutrals. Sans-only → sans plus mono for all data. Flat stays flat, but depth comes from layered surface steps.
- **Alerts:** An alert takes over its surface. It shows one clear action and a strong status colour, with nothing decorative in the way.

## 2. Color Palette & Roles
- **Deep Bay** (#0A1013): The canvas, the deepest surface. Never pure black.
- **Bay Panel** (#0F181C): Raised surface for panels, table bodies and side navigation.
- **Bay Lift** (#15222727 is not used; use #152227): The top surface step for open menus, sheets, the selected row and the pass card.
- **Hairline** (rgba(196,228,240,0.09)): All 1px structural rules, table row dividers and panel edges.
- **Hairline Strong** (rgba(196,228,240,0.18)): Input borders, the active table header rule and inset rules on the pass card.
- **Signal Ink** (#E3ECEF): Primary text, plate numbers and key figures.
- **Instrument Grey** (#8B9CA3): Secondary text, labels and metadata.
- **Dim Grey** (#56676E): Disabled text, placeholder text and axis ticks.
- **Bay Cyan** (#2BA8D6): The single accent. It appears as thin lines, small fills, the primary button, the selected tab indicator, progress bars and the focus ring. It never fills a large area.
- **Cyan Wash** (rgba(43,168,214,0.12)): Selected row tint and pressed tint.
- **Status Clear** (#3FB57A): Green-light entry granted and space available. Used only for status.
- **Status Halt** (#E04A4F): Fail-closed alerts, denied entry and destructive confirmations. Used only for status.
- **Status Hold** (#D6A13C): Warnings: release pending or a directory lookup that is slow.

Status colours always come with a text label and a shape (a dot, a bar or an icon). Colour never carries meaning on its own.

## 3. Typography Rules
- **Display / Headlines:** IBM Plex Sans, weights 500–600. Tracking −0.02em at 28px and above. The scale is controlled: page title 24px, section title 16px/600. Hierarchy comes from weight and colour, not size.
- **Body:** IBM Plex Sans 400, 14px with 1.5 line height (16px minimum on mobile). Maximum line length is 65ch in Instrument Grey.
- **Mono:** IBM Plex Mono, used for every number, licence plate, floor and space code, time, date and count. Always set `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`. Plates are set in uppercase with +0.04em tracking.
- **Labels:** IBM Plex Sans 500 at 11px, uppercase, +0.08em tracking, in Instrument Grey.
- **Key fact:** One per view (your space, your floor, the live free count), set in IBM Plex Mono 500 at clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem) with −0.02em tracking.
- **Craft:** Use curly quotes, en dashes for ranges (08:00–18:00, 3–9 Oct) and a true ellipsis. Dates follow the locale (Mon 6 Oct 2025, 24-hour time). The page's one typographic contrast is mono figures set against sans words.
- **Banned:** Inter, generic serifs, and any serif anywhere in this product.

## 4. Component Stylings
- **Buttons:** Sharp 4px radius and 40px height (44px tap target on mobile). The primary button is a Bay Cyan fill with Deep Bay text, and there is only one per view. The secondary button is a Hairline Strong outline with Signal Ink text. Destructive actions use a Status Halt outline, which fills only inside the confirmation step. Hover tints the fill 6% lighter and nudges the trailing arrow 3px. Active is `scale(0.97)` at 90ms. There is never a glow and the CTA never pulses. Labels are product verbs ("Release today", "Claim a space", "Export CSV"), never "Get started".
- **Panels / Cards:** A surface step (Bay Panel on Deep Bay) with a 1px Hairline edge and a 4px radius. No shadow. Panels are used only where grouping matters. Lists and tables use row dividers instead.
- **Pass card:** Bay Lift with a 1px Hairline Strong inset rule and a 3px Bay Cyan top line. The key fact (floor and space) is set large in mono, with the plate and date beneath. This is the shared element that carries from a list to its detail view.
- **Tables:** Rows are 36px high with Hairline dividers. Headers are uppercase labels on a sticky Bay Panel with a Hairline Strong bottom rule. Numeric columns are right-aligned mono. Row hover is a Cyan Wash tint. The selected row gets a 2px Bay Cyan left rule. Sorting is shown with a small chevron at 1.5 stroke.
- **Status chips:** A square 6px dot plus a mono uppercase label at 11px on a 10% tint of the status colour. 2px radius.
- **Alert banner (fail-closed):** A full-width band of Status Halt at 14% tint with a 2px Status Halt left rule. It states the plate, the reason and one action. It does not auto-dismiss.
- **Inputs:** The label sits above in uppercase label style. The field is Deep Bay with a 1px Hairline Strong border, 4px radius and 40px height. Focus is a 2px Bay Cyan ring offset by 2px. Helper text sits below in Instrument Grey. Error text sits below in Status Halt and the border turns Status Halt. Plate inputs are mono uppercase. There are no floating labels.
- **Selectors (vehicle, date):** Segmented rows with a 1px Hairline. The selected item gets a Bay Cyan 1px border and a Cyan Wash fill.
- **Loaders:** Skeleton bars matching the exact row and figure dimensions, shimmering in Bay Lift. No spinners.
- **Empty states:** A short line of real guidance and the one action that fills the view (for example "No vehicles yet. Add the plate you park with."). Drawn with a single hairline outline glyph, not an illustration.
- **Errors:** Inline, next to the cause. Recoverable errors offer a Retry action and the support contact.

## 5. Layout Principles
- The layout is built on a 12-column CSS grid with a maximum width of 1400px and a 24px gutter. Desktop navigation is a fixed 232px left rail on Bay Panel and content starts at column 1 of the remaining area. Detail views split 8/4: the record on the left and its context (vehicles, assignment) on the right.
- Employee views on mobile are a single column with the key fact at the top and the primary action within thumb reach.
- Section rhythm varies: a key-fact band, then a dense table, then a narrow settings column. Sections never repeat the same template.
- There are no overlapping elements and no absolute stacking. Full-height areas use `min-h-[100dvh]`.
- Spacing follows a 4px base: 8, 12, 16 and 24 inside panels, and clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem) between sections.
- **Responsive:** Below 768px everything collapses to one column. The rail becomes a top bar with a menu sheet. Tables become stacked rows with the key value right-aligned. There is no horizontal scroll, and all touch targets are at least 44px.
- **Sign-in:** Left-aligned and asymmetric: product name, one line of purpose and one Google sign-in button on the left third, with an empty Deep Bay field crossed by a single hairline grid on the right. No hero imagery.

## 6. Motion & Interaction
Motion is fast and exact. Numbers roll to their values, lines and progress bars draw in, the pass carries from a list to its detail, rows insert with a short shift, and one live element breathes. Only `transform`, `opacity` and `clip-path` are animated. Each reveal happens once and then stays. All motion tokens and keyframes are in §9.

## 7. Anti-Patterns (Banned)
- No emojis.
- No Inter and no serif fonts.
- No pure black: the darkest surface is Deep Bay #0A1013.
- No glow, neon, gradient blobs, aurora, glass blur, purple-to-blue gradients or gradient text.
- No shadows beyond the surface steps.
- No 3-equal-card rows, no 4 KPI cards with sparklines, no bento grids and no pill badges.
- No sparkle icons.
- No "Get started" CTAs.
- No icons on every nav item: text carries the meaning, and icons appear only for status and the vehicle and alert glyphs.
- No placeholder names or fake round numbers: data uses real-looking plates, floors and counts.
- No AI copy clichés ("Elevate", "Seamless", "Unleash", "Next-Gen").
- No "Scroll to explore", scroll arrows or bouncing chevrons.
- No custom cursors.
- No pulsing buttons, bouncing elements or typewriter text.
- No parallax or scroll-jacking.
- No fly-ins, and no fade-up applied to every section.

## 8. Voice & Font Rationale
- **Voice:** exact, watchful, calm.
- **Display:** IBM Plex Sans, an engineered grotesk with industrial roots whose squared curves suit a control instrument without looking sci-fi (fallback: Hanken Grotesk).
- **Body / Mono:** IBM Plex Sans for body text, with IBM Plex Mono for plates, counts and times. Plex Mono's open zero and distinct 1/I/l make licence plates unambiguous at a glance.

## 9. Motion System
- **Tokens:**
  - Durations: `--dur-instant` 90ms, `--dur-quick` 160ms, `--dur-base` 260ms, `--dur-slow` 420ms, `--dur-scene` 800ms.
  - `--ease-out`: cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1).
  - `--ease-in`: cubic-bezier(0.7, 0, 0.84, 0). Exits are about 30% faster than entrances.
  - `--ease-inout`: cubic-bezier(0.65, 0, 0.35, 1).
  - `--ease-spring`: the `linear()` spring defined in the CSS block below.
  - `--travel`: 8px.
- **Entrance:** The page title, then the key fact, then the first panel reveal with opacity plus an 8px rise, staggered 60ms, all done within 800ms. Tables reveal as one group.
- **Scroll-linked:** Report bars and occupancy bars draw from scaleX(0) to their value on `animation-timeline: view(); animation-range: entry 0% entry 40%`. Each draws once and carries meaning: it is the share of capacity used.
- **Interaction feedback:**
  - Buttons: hover tint plus a 3px arrow nudge at 160ms; press `scale(0.97)` at 90ms.
  - Table rows: Cyan Wash tint at 160ms.
  - Nav links: a 2px left rule draws with scaleY 0→1.
  - Inputs: the focus ring fades in at 90ms.
  - Mobile list items: pressed tint is immediate.
- **State transitions:**
  - Tabs: the 2px Bay Cyan indicator slides between tabs at 260ms `--ease-inout`.
  - Accordions: `grid-template-rows: 0fr → 1fr` at 260ms.
  - New entry-log rows: insert with a 160ms fade and an 8px downward shift.
  - Pass card: shares a `view-transition-name: pass` from the list to its detail view.
  - Mobile sheets: rise at 420ms `--ease-out` while the backdrop fades to 40%.
  - Screen changes: push 24px with a fade.
- **Ambient (max 1):** The live-status dot beside the entrance check's "Live" label breathes. Its 1px ring scales 1→1.25 and its opacity goes 1→0.95 on a 6s `--ease-inout` infinite cycle. It appears on no other screen.
- **Signature moment:** "Count settles." The free-space count (and any other key-fact figure) rolls from 0 to its real value. Each tabular digit is a vertical translateY strip running over 600ms on `--ease-spring`, and as it lands, a 1px Bay Cyan rule beneath it draws from scaleX(0) to scaleX(1) at 260ms.
- **Reduced motion:** Under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`, entrances become instant opacity changes. Digits show their final value immediately. Bars render at their full value. The breathing dot is static. State changes keep at most a 120ms fade. No content is hidden while waiting for an animation.

```css
:root{
  --dur-instant:90ms; --dur-quick:160ms; --dur-base:260ms; --dur-slow:420ms; --dur-scene:800ms;
  --ease-out:cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1);
  --ease-in:cubic-bezier(0.7,0,0.84,0);
  --ease-inout:cubic-bezier(0.65,0,0.35,1);
  --ease-spring:linear(0,0.009,0.035 2.1%,0.141,0.281 6.7%,0.723 12.9%,0.938 16.7%,1.017,1.077 21.4%,1.121 24%,1.149 27%,1.159,1.154 33%,1.051 43.2%,1.013 49.5%,0.996 57%,1.001 72%,1);
  --travel:8px;
  --bay-cyan:#2BA8D6; --deep-bay:#0A1013; --bay-panel:#0F181C; --bay-lift:#152227;
}
@keyframes rise{from{opacity:0;transform:translateY(var(--travel))}to{opacity:1;transform:none}}
@keyframes digit-roll{from{transform:translateY(0)}to{transform:translateY(calc(var(--d) * -1em))}}
@keyframes rule-draw{from{transform:scaleX(0)}to{transform:scaleX(1)}}
@keyframes row-in{from{opacity:0;transform:translateY(-8px)}to{opacity:1;transform:none}}
@keyframes breathe{0%,100%{transform:scale(1);opacity:1}50%{transform:scale(1.25);opacity:.95}}
.reveal{animation:rise var(--dur-slow) var(--ease-out) both;animation-delay:calc(var(--i) * 60ms)}
.digit-strip{animation:digit-roll 600ms var(--ease-spring) both;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
.count-rule{transform-origin:left;animation:rule-draw var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out) 600ms both;height:1px;background:var(--bay-cyan)}
.bar{transform-origin:left;animation:rule-draw linear both;animation-timeline:view();animation-range:entry 0% entry 40%}
.log-row-new{animation:row-in var(--dur-quick) var(--ease-out)}
.live-dot::after{animation:breathe 6s var(--ease-inout) infinite}
.pass-card{view-transition-name:pass}
.btn:active{transform:scale(.97);transition:transform var(--dur-instant) var(--ease-out)}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){
  *{animation:none!important;transition:opacity 120ms linear!important}
}
```

## 10. Component Substitutions
- **4 KPI cards with sparklines:** replaced by one key-fact figure with its context line, then a dense sortable table.
- **"Trusted by" strips and stats rows:** omitted entirely.
- **Feature cards with icon tiles:** replaced by plain labelled rows with the value in mono.
- **Pill "New" badges:** replaced by a mono date line when needed (for example "Updated 06 Oct 09:14").
- **Glass or gradient backgrounds:** replaced by three solid tinted surface steps and hairlines.
- **Default shadcn look:** replaced by a sharp 2–4px radius system and a cyan 2px offset focus ring.
- **Icons on every nav link:** replaced by text navigation, with icons only for status, vehicles and alerts.
- **Mega footer:** replaced by a single-line footer with support contact and version in mono.
- **"Get started" CTAs:** replaced by product verbs.

## 11. Human Fingerprint
- **Unexpected decision:** Every space and floor code is set like a painted bay marking. It is mono uppercase inside a 1px Hairline Strong box with a 3px Bay Cyan top line, as if stencilled on the car park floor. The same mark appears on the pass, in tables and on the entrance check, tying the screens to the physical car park.
- **Radius family:** sharp, with 4px on buttons, inputs and panels and 2px on chips. Inner radius equals outer radius minus padding (minimum 0).
- **Elevation:** two levels (Bay Panel and Bay Lift) plus hairlines. Zero shadows.
- **Grid:** 12 columns, a 232px rail, an 8/4 split for detail views and a maximum width of 1400px.
- **Image treatment:** No photography. Visual weight comes from figures and rules. Avatars from the directory are 28px squares with a 2px radius and a 1px Hairline frame.
- **Icon set:** Lucide at 1.5 stroke, sizes 16 and 20 only, in Instrument Grey. Icons take a status colour only when they mark a status.
